WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.086 --> 00:00:05.505
♪♪

00:00:05.505 --> 00:00:07.007
Cherry:
Sometimes I feel like
I've already seen

00:00:07.007 --> 00:00:08.300
Cherry:
everything that's
gonna happen.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:10.010
♪♪

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:11.011
Cherry:
And it's a nightmare.

00:00:11.011 --> 00:00:12.971
(Loud explosion)

00:00:12.971 --> 00:00:13.972
Soldier:
Go, go!

00:00:13.972 --> 00:00:14.973
(Automatic gunfire)

00:00:14.973 --> 00:00:15.974
Soldier:
Go!

00:00:15.974 --> 00:00:16.975
♪♪

00:00:16.975 --> 00:00:21.104
This is a movie that is based
upon a young man who makes
a really important decision to

00:00:21.104 --> 00:00:22.856
Joe Russo:
join the Army during the Iraq
war.

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:29.196
The shock that he experiences in
Iraq is something that he can't
shake for the rest of the film.

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:30.864
(Mirror shattering)

00:00:30.864 --> 00:00:32.491
He comes back with undiagnosed
PTSD.

00:00:32.866 --> 00:00:34.284
Tom Holland:
It's an invisible affliction.

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:36.537
People see someone with PTSD and
go

00:00:36.537 --> 00:00:38.538
"Oh that guy is fine, he came
home and he wasn't injured."

00:00:38.747 --> 00:00:40.332
I have this noise in my head.

00:00:40.916 --> 00:00:41.917
It'll stop.

00:00:41.917 --> 00:00:44.253
Emily:
One day it'll just go quiet.

00:00:44.253 --> 00:00:46.046
♪♪

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:48.048
Timothy Wynn:
I came home from Iraq in 2003.

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:51.885
My family, friends, they had no
idea really what was going on
internally with me.

00:00:51.885 --> 00:00:53.053
♪♪

00:00:53.053 --> 00:00:57.724
When you're coming out of a
combat zone, it is very jarring
to return to the civilian world.

00:00:57.724 --> 00:01:00.727
You don't want to talk about it
sometimes, you don't want to go
through it again.

00:01:00.727 --> 00:01:02.062
♪♪

00:01:02.062 --> 00:01:04.064
Anthony Russo:
The medical system
was unprepared to

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.482
Anthony Russo:
help Cherry
with these issues.

00:01:05.482 --> 00:01:06.692
How's your pain level?

00:01:06.692 --> 00:01:07.693
Nine out of ten.

00:01:07.693 --> 00:01:08.944
Have you ever
heard of oxycontin?

00:01:09.486 --> 00:01:11.280
They mis-prescribe opioids.

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:13.365
Anthony Russo:
And that turns into a bad
addiction for him.

00:01:13.365 --> 00:01:15.242
Anthony Russo:
And that ends up turning into a
life of crime.

00:01:15.242 --> 00:01:16.910
(Gunshots)
Get on the ground now!

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:17.911
♪♪

00:01:17.911 --> 00:01:20.914
Living with PTSD took me to some
pretty dark places.

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:21.915
♪♪

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:23.917
Timothy Wynn:
I was addicted to drugs and
alcohol and spent a year

00:01:23.917 --> 00:01:24.918
Timothy Wynn:
of my life in prison.

00:01:25.711 --> 00:01:28.714
Every week there was a younger
version of me walking through
those doors.

00:01:28.714 --> 00:01:29.756
♪♪

00:01:29.756 --> 00:01:34.094
We have lost family members, we
have others who are struggling
with their sobriety.

00:01:34.094 --> 00:01:35.095
♪♪

00:01:35.095 --> 00:01:37.597
There is a scale to this that is
terrifying.

00:01:37.723 --> 00:01:38.724
(Incoherent screaming)

00:01:38.724 --> 00:01:39.725
♪♪

00:01:39.725 --> 00:01:41.101
Honorable Patrick Murphy:
There's about 3.3 million
of us that

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:43.103
Honorable Patrick Murphy:
served in Iraq and Afghanistan.

00:01:43.103 --> 00:01:46.273
Honorable Patrick Murphy:
And there still are far too many
that do fall thru the cracks.

00:01:46.273 --> 00:01:48.108
Honorable Patrick Murphy:
Sometimes they give up hope.

00:01:48.108 --> 00:01:50.193
That's why it's important to
tell these stories.

00:01:50.193 --> 00:01:51.194
♪♪

00:01:51.194 --> 00:01:55.699
A movie like Cherry helps all of
us to understand that it's okay
to reach out for help.

00:01:55.699 --> 00:01:59.119
Jimmy Butler:
And we, as a country, can begin
this healing process together.

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:00.120
♪♪

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:01.121
You're it for me.

00:02:01.121 --> 00:02:02.122
I feel the same way.

00:02:02.414 --> 00:02:05.625
Cherry represents the
possibility of a bright future.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:08.128
♪♪

00:02:08.128 --> 00:02:12.341
I believe this film is gonna
help people, and get the
struggle out to the masses.

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:16.678
They showed the grit of not just
combat, but coming back on the
other side.

00:02:16.678 --> 00:02:17.679
♪♪

00:02:17.679 --> 00:02:20.724
There are so new many therapies
that are out there, it's gonna
be different

00:02:20.724 --> 00:02:22.309
for all of us, we have to
understand that.

00:02:22.309 --> 00:02:23.310
♪♪

00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:24.686
Jimmy Butler:
But hope is a mandatory.

00:02:25.062 --> 00:02:28.065
We have to do everything we can
to make sure that we leave
no-one behind.

00:02:28.607 --> 00:02:32.861
We owe it to the ones that did
not come back to live a happy
and healthy life.

00:02:32.861 --> 00:02:33.862
♪♪

00:02:33.862 --> 00:02:36.531
Tom Holland:
The service men and women here
today really are unparalleled

00:02:36.531 --> 00:02:38.325
and we're indebted to them in
every way.

00:02:38.325 --> 00:02:39.534
♪♪

00:02:39.534 --> 00:02:41.161
Cherry:
Sometimes I feel like I've
already seen

00:02:41.161 --> 00:02:42.371
Cherry:
everything that's
gonna happen.

00:02:42.371 --> 00:02:43.413
♪♪

00:02:43.413 --> 00:02:46.083
Cherry:
But for the first time, it
didn't scare me.

00:02:46.083 --> 00:02:48.835
♪♪

